From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 00:35:36 +0200
Subject: usb: musb: Add Allwinner A64 USB-OTG internal DMA support

Offload bulk host<->device transfers on the A64 MUSB to the Allwinner
"internal DMA" engine instead of PIO, in both directions. With this,
g_mass_storage runs at ~42 MB/s (USB-HS line rate).

The DMA engine's specifics that were discovered during implementation:

* idma has no separate IRQ line: completion is polled from
  sunxi_musb_interrupt() before calling musb_interrupt()

* VEND0 (0x43) is a global PIO/DMA select for the FIFO datapath, not
  per-endpoint. It must be switched to DMA around a transfer and back to
  PIO once no channel is busy, or interleaved PIO traffic (mass-storage
  CBW/CSW, ep0, short packets) is routed to the DMA interface and
  breaks.

* DMA_BC is NOT a residual counter. After completion it reads back the
  programmed byte count, so "len - residual" is always 0. The engine
  raises a single completion only once the whole programmed (whole-
  packet) transfer is done, so we report the programmed length as
  actual_len.

* Whole maxpackets only. is_compatible() rejects <= maxpacket transfers
  so CBWs, short SCSI status, control transfers and any sub-packet tail
  stay on PIO; channel_program rounds the length down to whole packets.

* RX needs the Mode 1 CSR setup (AUTOCLEAR | DMAENAB, DMAMODE toggled);
  the Mentor "Mode 0" setup leaves AUTOCLEAR clear and the engine moves
  nothing. f_mass_storage does not set short_not_ok, so a new gadget-RX
  behavior quirk (MUSB_DMA_RX_MODE1_ALWAYS) makes rxstate() force Mode 1
  for any full-packet DMA-mapped transfer.

* TX is order-sensitive: the idma START bit begins moving data
  immediately, so the full TXCSR DMA config (AUTOSET|MODE|DMAENAB|
  DMAMODE) is programmed before START rather than after (where txstate
  writes it). The completion also fires while the last packet is still
  in the Tx FIFO; musb_g_tx() clears TxPktRdy on completion, which would
  drop it, so we wait (time-bounded) for the FIFO to drain before
  reporting completion.

* EP1 bulk FIFO is double-buffered (2x512, TX and RX) so the controller
  can hold/accept the next packet while the engine drains/fills the
  current one. This helps get the performance of USB storage function
  to the line rate, when it is configured on EP1.

Allwinner SoC families are a babylon of small quirks and changes, so
all of this is in this initial commit targeted at A64 SoC, to avoid
breaking any other SoC I did not yet test, or have access to.

I added a new A64 specific compatible "allwinner,sun50i-a64-musb" for
this purpose. Existing A64 DTs that are using "allwinner,sun8i-a33-musb"
keep running on PIO. People who upgrade their DTs along with their
kernels will be the lucky ones. :)

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
